==================================================
73. OBSERVABILITY INVARIANTS
==================================================

The following are canonical:

1. Observe the system, not the person.

2. Observability is not Memory.

3. Observability is not Context.

4. Observability is not surveillance.

5. Logs must be data-minimized.

6. Metrics should be preferred for aggregate behavior.

7. Traces must avoid unnecessary user content.

8. Secrets must never be logged.

9. Sensitive data must be redacted or excluded.

10. Telemetry must have a classification.

11. Telemetry access requires authorization.

12. Retention must have a defined purpose.

13. User content should be accessed only when necessary.

14. Diagnostic mode must be controlled.

15. Remote telemetry must not become automatic user-data
    replication.

16. UNKNOWN must remain UNKNOWN.

17. Events, traces and metrics must support failure
    reconstruction.

18. Observability must remain compatible with Privacy & Security.

19. Observability must remain subordinate to Governance.

20. The system must remain diagnosable without requiring
    permanent surveillance of the user.

