==================================================
75. FINAL CANONICAL PRINCIPLE
==================================================

"PRSL-AI must be observable enough to explain and correct its
behavior, but must never require surveillance of the user's
private life to remain operationally trustworthy."

==================================================
76. FINAL STATEMENT
==================================================

Observability is what allows PRSL-AI to know what is happening
inside itself.

Events tell the ecosystem what occurred.

Metrics reveal patterns.

Logs explain operational conditions.

Traces reconstruct distributed execution.

Verification establishes whether results were actually achieved.

Audit preserves critical accountability.

Diagnostics investigate failures.

Privacy & Security determines what may be exposed.

Governance determines what may be collected and who may access
it.

Together, these mechanisms create a system that can explain
itself without continuously recording the person using it.

The canonical philosophy is therefore:

SEE THE SYSTEM.

UNDERSTAND THE FAILURE.

PROTECT THE USER.

DO NOT TURN DIAGNOSTICS INTO SURVEILLANCE.

